steps.text:
The figure of a biaxial stone depends on the <b>position of the stone</b> on the lens:

• <b>a</b>: both axes are in the field, the dark band forms a <b>cross</b> with two “eyes”;
• <b>b</b>: the stone turned by 45°, the cross has opened into a <b>moustache</b>, two curved branches around the eyes;
• <b>c</b>: only one axis is in the field: you see just one curved branch and a single eye.

With an auxiliary plate, you also read the <b>optic sign</b>, positive or negative: it is the same as the one of the refractometer.
